  "text": "(1) wood pellets; (2) platform and intermediate chemicals (emerging bioproducts), as well as conventional bioproducts; (3) lignin; and (4) biochar. A 2023 USDA report evaluated multiple biobased products including agriculture and forestry, biorefining, bio-based chemicals, enzymes, bioplastic bottles and packaging, forest products, and textiles as the seven major bio-based product industries contributing to the U.S. economy. It specifically excluded contributions to the economy from energy, livestock, food, feed, and pharmaceuticals. The USDA report stated that bio-based products accounted for 3.9 million jobs and a $489 billion contribution to the economy (Golden et al. 2024). 1 E15 is a blend of 10.5%–15% ethanol and gasoline; E85 is an ethanol-gasoline blend containing 51%–83% ethanol, depending on geography and season. 2 The National Laboratory of the Rockies purchases vehicle registration data from Experian and compared the total number of vehicles versus model year 2001 and newer: www.experian.com/automotive/auto-vehicle-data. viii This report is available at no cost from the National Laboratory of the Rockies at www.nlr.gov/publications. Table of Contents Executive Summary ..................................................................................................................................... v 1 Biomass to Bioenergy Overview ......................................................................................................... 1 2 Biofuels .................................................................................................................................................. 3 2.1 Biofuels Industry Drivers ............................................................................................................... 3 2.2 Feedstocks ...................................................................................................................................... 5 2.3 Economic Impacts and Jobs ............................